With regards to your message at 11:37 AM 2/28/01, KirkE@paccessglobal.com. 
Where you stated:
>Nikos,
>
>UP2000 and UP2000 plus use the same Tsunami 21272 chipset (83.5MHz, 300+MHz
>system interface, memory point to point ports from 128 bits to 256bits) as
...

Nice description Kirk!
Probably the clearest and most thorough quick encapsulation of these boards 
I have seen.

There is so much bad information bandied around.

BTW, the DP264 is now end of life. API sent out formal announcements last week.
Also the EV67 SlotB are EOL too.
EV68 in 667 and 833, both with 4MB DDR is the current offering.
Also, the CS-20 is now shipping finally, albeit in small quantities.
Also EV68, DDR.

Lastly, the UP1500 is supposed to becoming in March. Basically the UP1100, 
but UDMA100, 2GB RAM capacity, and a few other tweaks.

