On Sunday 04 March 2001 14:52, Peter Watkinson wrote:
> How about Mozilla that's some kind of web browser isn't it?

Sure.  It is the Netscape 6.0 code.

> It's also at the Rawhide site. has anyone tried it?

Not for awhile.  I was running short of space in the partition I usually 
compile in and the last Mozilla required +500Meg to compile.  It is supposed 
to be much better with the last milestone.  

Kde2.1 has mozilla bindings to use that as the html rendering engine.  
Basically you should be able to run mozilla inside of konq for any html type 
stuff if you want.

