Hello,

On Mon, 19 Mar 2001, Andrei A. Dergatchev wrote:
> 
> He said that he successfully used 4K sector size for testings.
> But, as it was stated in this thread too, Linux does not support
> any sector size different from 512 bytes yet.
	Well I am not so sure about the 512 byte limitation. My mo-drive
works under linux, and the platters sport 2048 byte sectors. (This is a
HARD limit, no scsi command is likely to change that ;)) I can write to
it, I can read from it, so I assume it works (I have not noticed any
file corruption, but I did not really check for it either).
	The biggest catch seems to be that the choice of filesystems that
support blocks larger than 512 is somewhat limited. (Judging from man
mount on SuSE 6.3). (Number two might be fdisk...)	

Ahoi
	Sebastian Moeller

DISCLAIMER: As usual I do not really have any clue, nor do I tell the
truth, so anybody please correct me where I err.




