speed of 5400 RPM, and they cost a packet too -- all for 1.6GB.  Them were the
days.  I remember thinking how anyone would fill up a 10MB HD in my first PC.  And
then along came bloatware and solved that problem.  And the drives got bigger, and
there was much rejoicing.  And lo, a leviathan did appear, and it was to be called
MP3, and verily it begat DivX, and there was much gnashing of teeth.  And then Max
of Tor made proclamation of Diamonds and there were 80 GB available to the masses.
And then some sysadmin did scream, "How the bloody hell am I gonna back up this
little lot ?!".
But I digest....


