> seems like it blocks in some osf_gettimeofday calls.
>
> If, as user, I try sudo netscape, then I get a window, but nothing
> more. If a click the Home icon it hangs up in "Looking up host ...". Stop,
> Esc, nothing helps anymore.

Hello,
I remember having had the same problem. In the end it was a missing entry in 
the /etc/resolv.conf file. In fact you have to have a line saying 
search <your server>
so, in your case perhaps
search tu-cottbus.de
Sometimes there is also en entry missing in the /etc/hosts to properly look 
up YOUR host.
Anyway, here I have the problem that I can ping the hosts in /etc/hosts under 
root, but not under user... damned!

Greets

Ineiti




